Liberation Sans, Serif and Mono (Debian fonts-liberation, https://github.com/liberationfonts), SIL OFL 1.1 (LICENSE).
Built into webby.wasm (Resources.c) so pages and the chrome have fonts on any host, NixOS included, and with no
directories opened to the module.

WebbySymbols.ttf: the symbol blocks (U+2010-2BFF: punctuation, arrows, math, technical, shapes, symbols, dingbats)
of DejaVu Sans (Debian fonts-dejavu-core), renamed so it never stands in for a real "DejaVu Sans"; Bitstream Vera /
DejaVu license (LICENSE.DejaVu). Pages and the chrome fall back to it for symbols Liberation lacks (✦ ✕ ▾ ★ ✓ ⋮).
Remake: pyftsubset DejaVuSans.ttf --unicodes=U+2010-2BFF --layout-features='*' --no-hinting --desubroutinize,
then set name IDs 1/4/16 to "Webby Symbols" and 6 to "WebbySymbols".
